{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 22,
      "name": "Sticky Walls",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "A section is just a few walls, a gap and a slide speed, so each one is quick to place by hand and tune by feel. A generator would mostly give the same corridor with other numbers, and wall-jump distances need a playtest per layout anyway.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "Parts with a look, size and position (walls are plain slabs)",
          "slide motion: a wall that moves in and out, a red drop that slides down a wall",
          "flip motion and its duty beat (reusable as the beat for goo that dries)",
          "red see-through hazard parts: touch = back to the start pad",
          "JellyWallHop and StickyLadder already put jelly walls and climbable goo in the course (look and layout code to borrow)",
          "ObbyCourse.spec gap and rise checks (GAP_MAX 6, RISE_MAX 3.5, launch reach maths)",
          "Climb (idea 8) already plans the red drop prop, the 'grab' test step kind and the longer section cap; Vine Swing (15) and Aim the Cannon (26) plan the shared 'held by a prop, jump lets go' client base"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "Client sticky-wall controller: touching a sticky wall in the air holds you on it and slides you down at that wall's speed; Jump throws you off, up and away from the wall, steered forward by your stick. Build it on the same 'held by a prop, jump lets go' client base as Vine Swing's grab controller (15) and Aim the Cannon's cannon seat controller (26), with the same short no-grab time after letting go. Must work with the default Humanoid and on phone (Jump button = let go).",
            "size": "L"
          },
          {
            "what": "Sticky wall look: flat dripping green goo sheet with handprints (Climb, idea 8, keeps the open rung lattice so the two never look alike), a squelch when you stick, a slime trail while you slide; plain walls look like plain stone",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Per-wall settings: slide speed, sticky patches (only part of a wall grips), and a wet/dry beat (goo turns grey, you slide straight off) timed by Beat Pads' BeatClock (idea 18) so the tick before it dries is in time",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Dries when you stick: Melting Floor's melt trigger and melt warning look (idea 2, the same one Climb's Crumbling Rungs uses) on a goo patch: it greys and cracks 1 s after you stick, comes back after a few seconds",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Moving walls and windows use the 'shuttle' slide (ideas 3 and 25: hold, move, hold) instead of a plain sine, so 'close' and 'lined up' last long enough to read",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Red drops on walls: reuse Climb's drip motion kind and drop prop (idea 8) placed against the wall face, not a second drop",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "Test rule for wall chains: a 'wall' step kind built on Climb's 'grab' step kind (reach to a wall face, not a floor) plus the shared launch reach check (Bounce Chain 4 / Speed Strip 16) for the jump-off arc: wall-to-wall gaps and height gained or lost per hop",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "Hazard touch = back to the start pad (the shared one from idea 1)",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "Only dripping green goo with handprints is sticky; plain stone next to it is not. A squelch when you stick and a slime trail while you slide tell you that you are on the wall and how fast you are going down.",
      "generator": null,
